        "text": "Analyze this soil report image and extract ONLY the following values:\n\n- pH\n- Nitrogen (N)\n- Phosphorus (P)\n- Potassium (K)\n- Electrical Conductivity (EC)\n- Moisture\n\nRules:\n\n1. If the image is NOT a valid soil report OR the text is unreadable/blurred/failed OCR OR the required values cannot be identified confidently, return ONLY:\n\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Invalid soil report or OCR failed\"\n}\n\n2. If the image is a valid soil report and values are detected, return STRICT JSON in this exact format:\n\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"ph\": \"\",\n  \"nitrogen\": \"\",\n  \"phosphorus\": \"\",\n  \"potassium\": \"\",\n  \"ec\": \"\",\n  \"moisture\": \"\"\n}\n\n3. If some fields are missing but the report is still valid, keep success=true and set missing fields to null.\n\nExample:\n\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"ph\": \"6.8\",\n  \"nitrogen\": null,\n  \"phosphorus\": \"34\",\n  \"potassium\": \"120\",\n  \"ec\": \"0.45\",\n  \"moisture\": null\n}\n\n4. Return ONLY raw JSON.\n5. Do NOT add markdown.\n6. Do NOT add explanations.\n7. Do NOT add extra fields.\n8. Do NOT return text before or after JSON.",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "binaryPropertyName": "image",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
